# Open folder from OS Explorer / Finder

**Status:** ✅ DONE (v1) — Windows Explorer HKCU menu + launch-arg/`vigil://open` + macOS Open With (`public.folder`) + second process per folder with sidecar port isolation.  
**Related:** workspace `explorerStore.openWorkspace`, deep links `vigil://`, `.cursor/rules/00-الخطة-العامة-والأولويات.mdc`  
**Not this:** in-window project combo (cancelled in `07`) — another workspace is another Vigil **window/process** when architecture allows; v1 opens the folder in the running app.

---

> **عربي:** قصة المنتج

## 0. Product story

Right-click a project folder in Windows Explorer → **Open with Vigil** (same habit as Cursor). On Mac, **Open With → Vigil AI Agent** on a folder, or drop the folder on the Dock icon.

---

> **عربي:** إجابات مقفولة

## 1. Hard answers

| Question | Answer |
|----------|--------|
| Windows Explorer folder menu? | **Yes** — per-user `HKCU` (no admin) |
| Inside an open folder (background click)? | **Yes** — `Directory\Background` + `%V` |
| Right-click a file? | Open the **parent folder** as the workspace |
| macOS Finder? | **Yes, best-effort:** `public.folder` Open With + Dock drop. Full Finder Sync extension later |
| In-window project switcher? | **No** — cancelled (`07`) |
| Kashier / Secure PDF / EXE / Crystal | Separate tracks; EXE+Crystal+PDF reports stay lower than this desktop habit |

---

> **عربي:** تنفيذ

## 2. Implementation

- ✅ Parse CLI / `file://` / `vigil://open?path=` → folder (file → parent)  
- ✅ Frontend: `take_launch_open_path` on explorer init + `vigil://open-folder` while running  
- ✅ Windows: install/remove Explorer verbs from Settings → Appearance; auto-install on first Windows launch  
- ✅ macOS: Info.plist document type `public.folder`  
- [ ] NSIS installer duplicate of HKCU verbs (release polish)  
- ✅ Second Vigil process / window per folder (sidecar port isolation)

